# Polytonic Greek speech dictionary for Dutch TTS (Erasmian pronunciation).
# Transliterates polytonic Greek into Dutch-phonetic text before speech.
# Fields: pattern<TAB>replacement<TAB>caseSensitive<TAB>type
# type 0 = ANYWHERE, type 1 = REGEXP, type 2 = WORD,
# type 3 = PART_OF_WORD, type 4 = START_OF_WORD.
# Every word-initial (type 4) entry has a WORD (type 2) twin below it:
# type 4 requires a following word character, so it never matches when
# the pattern is a complete standalone word (frequent for articles).
# Uppercase forms match through case-insensitive folding unless listed.
# Known limitation: crasis forms (e.g. κἀγώ) carry a mid-word breathing
# and pass through untransliterated.
# Order matters: multi-char / breathing rules must precede single-char rules.

# ====================================================================
# Section 0: Punctuation needing Greek context (regex, type 1).
# Must run first, while the preceding character is still Greek.
# ASCII semicolon and middle dot also occur in other languages, so
# they are only converted directly after a Greek letter.
# ====================================================================
(?<=[\u0370-\u03FF\u1F00-\u1FFF]);	?	0	1
(?<=[\u0370-\u03FF\u1F00-\u1FFF])\u00B7	;	0	1

# ====================================================================
